<title>FRANCE: Paris Jan-Jun air cargo traffic higher.</title>
<headline>Paris Jan-Jun air cargo traffic higher.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Import traffic at the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 264,552 tonnes, in January-June 1997 or an increase of 3.2 percent on last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>Export traffic for Jan-Jun '97 from Charles de Gaulle and Orly, was 287,592 tonnes, a 1.9 percent rise on the same period.</p>
<p>The Paris airports January-June 1997 import and export traffic, in tonnes, by region, with percentage change on Jan-Jun 1996, were:</p>
<p>			  Imports		 Exports</p>
<p>Domestic		13,099 down 13.3    20,402 down  10.6</p>
<p>European Union	34,364   up 15.6    35,025   up   7.3</p>
<p>Non-EU Europe	  6,153   up 12.6     7,152   up  14.4</p>
<p>N. Africa		5,122 down 16.4     5,340   up   2.8</p>
<p>Sub-Saharan Africa  27,382 down  2.0    22,760   up   0.4</p>
<p>N. America	    85,605 down  6.6    13,312 down   0.1</p>
<p>French territories   7,112   up  9.8    80,385   up   4.3</p>
<p>LATAM		   10,704   up  8.6    15,941   up   5.6</p>
<p>Middle East	   12,402   up  0.2    27,985 down   0.1</p>
<p>Far East		62,609   up 21.6    59,290   up   0.3</p>
<p>Total		  264,552   up  3.2   287,592   up   1.9</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 1 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
